Difference:
    class: defines a data type (template / blueprint with attributes and methods)
        e.g. int, or Teacher
    object: an instance of a class, with its own values
        e.g. 42, 15, 99 are objects of int; wiltsu is an object of Teacher

UML relationships (FIX: the task asks for TWO possible relationships for each row):
1. transportation: Train, Passenger
   - aggregation: a Train has Passengers
   - dependency: a Passenger uses a Train
2. school: Student, Course
   - dependency: a Student uses (takes) Courses
   - aggregation: a Course has Students
3. interior design: Table, Furniture
   - inheritance: a Table is a Furniture
   - aggregation: a set of Furniture (e.g. a dining set) contains a Table
4. family: Parent, Child
   - aggregation: a Parent has Children
   - dependency: a Child uses (depends on) a Parent
   (FIX note: not inheritance - a Child is not a type of Parent)
5. library: Book, Literature
   - inheritance: a Book is a (piece of) Literature
   - aggregation: Literature (e.g. a collection) contains Books
